<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tang-e Sarvak</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tang-e Sarvak is a valley in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, known for rock reliefs carved on large boulders in the Parthian period. The reliefs show rulers and nobles of Elymais in Parthian dress, banqueting, hunting and receiving homage, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a> inscriptions, and are among the main monuments of the kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tang-e-sarvak.jpg" alt="Tang-e Sarvak" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davidplan66 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%86%D9%82%D9%88%D8%B4_%D8%A8%D8%AC%D8%B3%D8%AA%D9%87_%D9%87%D8%A7%DB%8C_%D8%AA%D9%86%DA%AF_%D8%B3%D8%B1%D9%88%DA%A9-_%D8%B3%D9%86%DA%AF_%D8%B3%D9%88%D9%85_%D8%AF%D9%88.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
